    "note": "Filed route text (from Alex's own FlightAware app): BARNR DLN295035/D030 BOI. Filed 375 kts, 28,000 ft, duration 1:35. Confirmed real: DLN = Dillon, MT VORTAC (45.2554N/112.5525W). BARNR omitted -- checked OpenNav (returns an empty shell page for this ident, not a real match), GlobalAir (403), and general FAA fix search; no reliable coordinate found, not guessed, same standard as VALYY/LYONS/TORIN on prior missions. The DLN295035/D030 hold (radial 295, 30nm, D0+30 legs) is plotted using DLN's real VOR coordinates with an approximate +12 degree magnetic-to-true correction (same method as the FCA/MSO and DTA holds on prior missions) -- this computed point falls squarely inside the real FDC TFR 6/1528 polygon (see tfrs below), which is strong independent corroboration the hold and the TFR are the same operation, not just a coincidence. **Corrected 2026-08-05 in-flight:** the filed line originally jumped straight from KBOI to the approximated hold point (bearing 45.4 deg from KBOI), but the real recorded track was flying a bearing of 57-61 deg -- almost exactly the direct bearing to the DLN VOR itself (55.9 deg), not the hold point. Standard IFR practice is direct-to-the-VOR first, then intercept the published radial into the hold, so this was the filed line missing a leg, not the aircraft deviating. Added the DLN VOR itself as an explicit leg before the hold point to match.",
    "pattern": "Departed KBOI 2026-08-05 16:19:42 UTC (10:19:42 AM MDT, confirmed by real ADS-B ground-roll points, not estimated), climbed out heading NE (track ~045) directly toward the Dillon/Beaverhead County target, flew a racetrack/survey pattern almost directly over Sand Creek and Bobcat Lakes for roughly an hour, then transited back to Boise and **landed at KBOI 2026-08-05 17:57:30 UTC (11:57:30 AM MDT)** -- confirmed both by the real ADS-B trace (globe.airplanes.live trace_full, re-pulled after landing) and independently by Claude's own dedicated live recorder (track_logs/nasa520_0805_live_recording.jsonl, polling every ~15s server-side, immune to any browser tab closing) which actually caught a few final-approach points past where the third-party trace cuts off (down to 2,725 ft vs the trace's 3,100 ft) -- both sources merged below for the most complete picture. Total flight time ~1h38m vs 1:35 filed. **Confirmed by Alex: both Sand Creek (1,400 ac, 0% contained, Beaverhead Co MT, 45.5547N/113.3257W) and Bobcat Lakes (1,829 ac, 0% contained, Beaverhead Co MT, 45.6368N/113.2039W) are the mission targets** -- both undetermined cause, both Type 3 IC, showing active group/single-tree torching and (Sand Creek) spotting per the latest ICS-209 reports, in dry (~22-23% RH) sunny conditions with light 4mph wind. Left active per standing instruction -- archiving is Alex's call, not automatic."
